      "text": "I’ve done the analysis and I’m back with the results 🙏🏻❤️\n\nWhat I see is that you’re caught between broken expectations and a deep inner feeling of emptiness. The recent events triggered something really painful in you, not just connected to this person, but to how you build intimacy and trust in general. Right now, you're in emotional chaos and unsure of where to go - both in your personal life and with money or work.\n\nYou’ve been trying to build relationships based on old patterns that were either pushed onto you or shaped by pain. Fear of being abandoned, the need to be needed at any cost, the urge to save or tolerate too much. You got stuck in a mindset like, “If I give everything, they won’t leave me” - but that’s just not how it works. Deep down, there's a belief that love has to be earned.\n\nNow the issues with work and money are getting worse too, because when your emotional foundation gets shaken, your sense of worth and stability goes with it. These areas are closely linked. If love disappears, it feels like everything else falls apart too.\n\nIt’s like you’re standing at a crossroads. Your soul is pulling one way, but fear and pain are pulling the other.\n\nEnergetically, I see blockages in your second and fourth chakras - sexuality, trust, openness, joy - all of that has tightened up. You’re not allowing yourself to be soft, loving, or fully expressed because you're scared it will just lead to more hurt.\n\nAnd your root chakra, the Muladhara, is underactive. That’s where issues with money, housing, and feeling safe in the world come from.\n\nThere’s also a family imprint, most likely passed down through the maternal line. Things like:\n“Men bring pain. Love is survival. It’s safer to be alone than broken again.”\nOr: “Don’t stick out. Don’t dream too big. Just settle for what you can get.”\nYou’re carrying that, even if you’re not aware of it.\n\nYour subconscious is whispering: “Love makes me vulnerable. It’s safer to be alone than to fall again.”\nAnd at the same time, it’s screaming: “I want to be loved. I want to feel alive, not just survive.”\n\nI also see an imbalance in how you give and receive - both in love and in money. You’ve gotten used to giving more than you get back. You’re afraid to ask, afraid to need anything. That blocks your flow - emotionally and materially.\n\nWhen someone avoids their true path for too long, the soul starts to speak through pain. It shows up in the body, in relationships, in career. If you don’t hear those signals now, life will keep creating situations of loss - not to punish you, but to wake you up and bring you back to yourself.\n\nBut the good news is: you have a real chance to shift all of this. I feel a light in you, a depth, a strength - and it can be activated. Everything happening right now isn’t a punishment. It’s a transition.\n\nYou can move through this. I’ve been there too - I lost everything once, had to start from scratch - and that moment became the turning point. I know how to guide you through this gently, clearly, and safely.\n\nWould you like me to tell you more about my practice which can help you with all of this?  🙏🏻",
