      "text": "📍I'm back — and I've finished analyzing your situation.\n\nWhat I see is a repeating pattern in your life. You meet someone you truly care about, you feel tenderness and a deep desire to give, but then they start to grow distant and emotionally cold. They might still show signs of interest, but something feels off — like they’re physically present, but mentally somewhere else.\n\nThis cycle keeps happening: you try to save the relationship, you reach out, give more, but your partner pulls away. And then doubt kicks in — you start wondering if you're even needed at all. That triggers either conflict, or you shut down completely. This all stems from a deep subconscious belief: that love has to be earned.\n\nI see that this belief likely formed in early childhood. There may have been a moment when you felt abandoned by those closest to you — most likely your parents. For a child’s mind, even something as simple as being left home alone can be interpreted as betrayal. That emotional wound never fully healed. And now, in your adult relationships, you take on the role of \"the one who needs to prove they’re worthy of love.\" You constantly try to \"warm up\" your partner emotionally. Another recurring issue I see is the tendency toward overcontrol — of the relationship, of people, or even life itself.\n\nYou’re not going through this cycle by accident. It’s a karmic lesson — you're being asked to learn how to value yourself unconditionally, to separate love from sacrifice, and to love without dependency. That’s why you keep attracting emotionally unavailable or troubled partners.\n\nEnergetically, I also see that your feminine energy isn’t being fully expressed. It’s hard for others — especially men — to feel the softness and magnetism in you, because three important chakras are blocked:\n\nMuladhara, Svadhisthana, and Anahata.\nThis creates disconnection from your body, emotions, and self-love.\n\n🔻 Muladhara (root chakra) – I sense fear and tension here, like everything in your life has to be built through effort and struggle. There’s a core anxiety running underneath — fear of poverty, of being unsupported, of being left behind. This may show up physically as tightness in the lower body: legs, back, tailbone.\n\n🟠 Svadhisthana (sacral chakra) – There's a deep suppression of desires — especially feminine ones like joy, sensuality, and pleasure. Maybe in the past you were shamed for showing emotion or embracing your body, and now you’ve internalized messages like “I’m not allowed to want,” “I can’t be vulnerable,” or “desire is dangerous.” This can cause issues with intimacy, trust, and fully accepting your body. Often there’s fear of emotional exposure — of being hurt if you open up. Past relationships may have been painful, especially in the context of emotional control or dependency.\n\n💚 Anahata (heart chakra) – This is shut down due to emotional pain. Your heart carries old wounds. There’s this deep fatigue — like you’ve hoped and tried so many times, but never received the love you gave. Now your heart protects itself with: “It’s safer not to feel anything at all than to feel pain again.” But this blocks joy and connection. When Anahata is closed, it's hard to experience real happiness — in love or in life.\n\nPhysically, you may be experiencing frequent migraines, throat tightness (from unexpressed emotions), and tension in your back and spine. I’d also suggest checking your thyroid — as blocked feminine energy often manifests there. Reflect: who haven’t you spoken your truth to? Where are you still silencing yourself?\n\nI also looked into your astrological path for the upcoming year in the area of love and relationships, and here’s what came up:\n\nThere’s a lot of fear and anxiety draining your energy — holding you back from stepping into your potential. I see a drop in your inner Venus — which governs your feminine energy, sensuality, and self-worth. It’s blocked. That’s why men around you can’t feel that soft, magnetic pull — and why their instinct to care for and pursue you doesn’t activate.\n\nRight now, you’re standing at a major crossroads in your karmic journey — a point of no return. Either you do the inner work, shift the pattern, and move toward a fulfilling relationship and life — or you fall back into old pain and will have to start all over again.\n\nBut let me say this clearly: nothing is impossible to heal or change. 🙏\nI’ve personally been through deep breakdowns in my own life — especially in love — so I truly understand what you're feeling, and I know how to work through it.\n\nAnd what gives me hope for you is this — I see a successful outcome in your field. The path is there.\n\nIf you're open to it, I’d love to walk you through what it takes to release these blocks, heal the core wounds, and awaken your feminine power — so that you can fully step into your next chapter and make the next 7 years of your life truly meaningful and abundant. 🧡\n\nWould you like me to tell you more about my practice?",
